FAILED missions/qc-concern-poi-provenance-modal-poi-provenance-js-2026-06-25.mission.txt <!-- 2026-07-07T16:32:13.851Z = RETRO-REPEAT-BLOCKED refusal mark, NOT a new attempt (gate correctly held it; the refusal clobbered the earlier stamp — restored here). FALSE-DEATH-JUDGED: GENUINE (0/6 Done-means markers at HEAD; stranded 40585b6 fails 5/7, not a pick candidate). FIX: requeue via fix-ledger recorded (class provenance-guard-rewrite-ready — on-disk text is the never-fired rewrite guarding the line-176 load-throw); PRECONDITION: preflight receipt newer than newest retro so the retro-gate admits the fire. Product-class, holds under GAP-PRIORITY-HOLD. FIX: none left to perform this beat — the requeue IS recorded+QUEUED; it fires when the hold lifts. | RESOLVED-BY-CONDUCTOR 2026-07-25 — 4 of the 5 real Done-means markers FIXED DIRECTLY (mission never re-run; the "fires when the hold lifts" disposition had silently expired, GAP-PRIORITY-HOLD is no longer set). All four commits deployed and live-verified (cache-busted; note muddytires.ca serves JS with Cache-Control max-age=14400, so a bare curl can show a stale copy): * MARKER 1 (loads outside a browser) — eb6ca77. Root cause was line 176 assigning window.mtOpenProvenance at TOP LEVEL, outside the file's own `typeof window !== 'undefined'` guard, so ANY non-browser load threw ReferenceError — reproduced before, exits 0 after. This one line was the runtimeVerify() gate that killed 5+ prior attempts and blocked every future mission touching this file. Fixed as a hoisted function declaration + export inside the existing guard; browser behaviour byte-identical. <!-- 2026-07-25T08:38:41.751Z * MARKER 3 (`if (!sourceName) return '';` gone) — 95b0a86. The early return hid the ENTIRE chip for community spots whose contributor is not public (functions/pois.json.js:285-294 nulls contributor_username and never emits a legacy `contributor` key), so those users also lost the freshness stamp, the confidence label AND the trust affordance — the least-attributable spots rendered as having nothing to disclose. Now falls back to the honest generic "community contributor". Verified across 4 provenance shapes with a stubbed window: curated + public-username output UNCHANGED, both anonymous cases went empty -> full chip. <!-- 2026-07-25T08:38:41.763Z * MARKER 4 (identifiers reachable without an inline handler) — b442531. The affordance was DEAD ON MOBILE: js/mobile-sheet.js's sanitiser strips event-handler attributes AND was dropping the data-mt-prov-* ids, so tapping the "i" did nothing on phones. Fixed with document-level click+keydown delegates on a[data-mt-prov-id] plus allowlisting the three INERT data attributes; onclick/onkeydown remain BANNED so the sanitiser's security property is unchanged. Verified with a sanitiser-shaped element: click intercepted, unrelated clicks pass through. <!-- 2026-07-25T08:38:41.800Z * MARKER 5 (mt-prov-css) — 5c38e99. Nothing in the repo defined .mt-prov-i (grep across *.css/*.html = 0), and the sheet strips inline style=, so the now-working control rendered as a bare unstyled "i". Injects an id-guarded <style> using the house pattern from js/poi-photos.js injectCSS, plus a :focus-visible ring it never had. Desktop unchanged (inline style survives and wins on specificity). <!-- 2026-07-25T08:38:41.824Z STILL OPEN — MARKER 2 ONLY, and it is NOT a defect: replacing the "i" glyph with a "How do we know?" TEXT affordance is a visible product/design decision, deliberately left to the operator. Do NOT requeue this mission to chase it; re-authoring as a fresh design mission with a Playwright receipt is the correct route (the stranded 40585b6 must never be cherry-picked — it adds a fresh inline onclick, regressing marker 4, and is dead on mobile for exactly the reason above). --> <!-- 2026-07-25T08:38:41.836Z -->
